From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Windows 7's sizes and bitmaps of linked fonts

Purpose: draw Japanese text in Latin UI faces (Tahoma, MS Shell Dlg 2,
Microsoft Sans Serif, Segoe UI) at Windows 7's size and with its
glyphs.
Windows behavior: a linked font is sized from the base font's em, also
when the base was asked for by cell height, and em 11 and 13 use the
linked font's 12 and 15 (Tahoma's 8 point Japanese is MS UI Gothic's 12
pixels). Sizes with embedded bitmaps are drawn with them, also in
ClearType text.
Wine before: the linked font took the base LOGFONT as is (the em, or the
cell height as the linked font's cell), and was drawn with the base
font's ClearType from the outline.
Change: in the Windows 7 shell, a child font asks for the base font's em
mapped as measured, and its embedded bitmap sizes load the bitmap for
gray and ClearType formats (the existing bitmap paths expand it).
Evidence: linkh.exe and linkq.exe on Windows 7 SP1 (Japanese, 96 dpi):
the linked glyph's advance for Tahoma, Microsoft Sans Serif and Segoe UI
from -40 to 30 pixels; linkd.exe: the glyphs in Tahoma -11 and -13 are
identical to MS UI Gothic's -12 and -15. In the session the advances
match from -40 to 30 apart from 1 and 2 pixels, and linkw.exe's
Japanese glyphs are identical to Windows 7.
Scope: the Windows 7 shell (WIN4WINE_SHELL=win7).
---
 dlls/win32u/font.c     | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 dlls/win32u/freetype.c |  9 ++++++++-
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/font.c b/dlls/win32u/font.c
index eb6a319..a2e2ac7 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/font.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/font.c
@@ -2751,15 +2751,27 @@ static UINT get_GSUB_vert_glyph( struct gdi_font *font, UINT glyph )
     return GSUB_apply_feature( font->gsub_table, font->vert_feature, glyph );
 }
 
+/* Windows 7 sizes a linked font from the base font's em, not its LOGFONT
+ * (a cell height asks for the base's em), and draws em 11 and 13 with the
+ * linked font's 12 and 15: measured on Windows 7 SP1 (Japanese, 96 dpi)
+ * with Tahoma, Microsoft Sans Serif and Segoe UI from 1 to 40 pixels, the
+ * glyphs identical to MS UI Gothic's at those sizes. */
+static int win7_linked_ppem( int ppem )
+{
+    return ppem == 11 ? 12 : ppem == 13 ? 15 : ppem;
+}
+
 static void add_child_font( struct gdi_font *font, const WCHAR *family_name )
 {
     FONTSIGNATURE fs = {{0}};
     struct gdi_font *child;
     struct gdi_font_face *face;
+    LOGFONTW lf = font->lf;
 
-    if (!(face = find_matching_face_by_name( family_name, NULL, &font->lf, fs, FALSE, NULL ))) return;
+    if (win4wine_shell() == WIN4WINE_SHELL_WIN7 && font->ppem > 0) lf.lfHeight = -win7_linked_ppem( font->ppem );
+    if (!(face = find_matching_face_by_name( family_name, NULL, &lf, fs, FALSE, NULL ))) return;
 
-    if (!(child = create_gdi_font( face, family_name, &font->lf ))) return;
+    if (!(child = create_gdi_font( face, family_name, &lf ))) return;
     child->matrix = font->matrix;
     child->can_use_bitmap = font->can_use_bitmap;
     child->scale_y = font->scale_y;
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/freetype.c b/dlls/win32u/freetype.c
index 32691a5..0e1136d 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/freetype.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/freetype.c
@@ -3217,7 +3217,14 @@ static UINT freetype_get_glyph_outline( struct gdi_font *font, UINT glyph, UINT
                    !(load_flags & FT_LOAD_NO_HINTING) && !has_bitmap_strike( font );
     if (xp_cleartype) load_flags = get_load_flags( GGO_BITMAP );
 
-    if (matrices || format != GGO_BITMAP) load_flags |= FT_LOAD_NO_BITMAP;
+    /* Windows 7 draws a linked font's sizes that have embedded bitmaps, such
+     * as MS UI Gothic's in Tahoma, with those bitmaps, also in ClearType or
+     * antialiased text (seen on Windows 7 SP1 with linkw.exe). */
+    if (font->base_font && !matrices && !vertical_metrics && !(load_flags & FT_LOAD_NO_HINTING) &&
+        format != GGO_BITMAP && format != GGO_METRICS && format != GGO_NATIVE && format != GGO_BEZIER &&
+        has_bitmap_strike( font ) && win4wine_shell() == WIN4WINE_SHELL_WIN7)
+        load_flags = get_load_flags( GGO_BITMAP );
+    else if (matrices || format != GGO_BITMAP) load_flags |= FT_LOAD_NO_BITMAP;
     if (vertical_metrics) load_flags |= FT_LOAD_VERTICAL_LAYOUT;
 
     err = pFT_Load_Glyph(ft_face, glyph, load_flags & FT_LOAD_NO_HINTING ? load_flags : load_flags | FT_LOAD_PEDANTIC);
